        {
          "class": "DepictionMarkdownView",
          "markdown": "**RoadRunner Reborn** makes your Now Playing app (and optionally other selected apps) stay alive through sbreload and resprings, keeping your music and other apps uninterrupted!\n\nTested on iOS 15 - 17 rootless, **should** work on rootHide and iOS 18 and newer (fingers crossed)",
          "useSpacing": true
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionSeparatorView"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionHeaderView",
          "title": "Changelog"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionMarkdownView",
          "markdown": "**1.1.6**\n\n- Apps that are meant to survive are captured more reliably.\n- Survivor handoff data is now stored properly in a plist instead of the temp directory.\n- Invalid survivor records are ignored instead of being restored.\n- SpringBoard and runningboardd coordinate so they do not overwrite each other’s changes.\n- Blacklist mode keeps its existing app list when iOS temporarily cannot provide a valid app list.\n- Missing process information no longer causes SpringBoard to crash randomly.\n- The system now-playing session is restored after resprings, so Dynamic Peninsula and lock screen cards recover without restarting the app.\n- Avoids sending a premature SpringBoard now-playing refresh before MediaRemote has a valid player path.",
          "useSpacing": true
        },
